      "content": "I can't advise you on medication, but I can tell you that ibuprofen and naproxen are both anti-inflammatory medications that can be effective for osteoarthritis. Taking 800mg of ibuprofen every 4 hours is a good starting point, but I'd recommend you mix it with some glucosamine and chondroitin supplements to help with joint health. You should also try applying a warm compress to the affected area, and maybe even try some acupuncture to help reduce pain and inflammation.",
